# =============================================================================
#  .gitignore
# =============================================================================
#  NOTE: ops-logs/*.txt is deliberately NOT ignored. The captured logs are the
#  whole point of this repo - committing them is how a run escapes a machine
#  nobody can reach. Don't "tidy" them into here.
#
#  NOTE: secrets/*.enc is deliberately NOT ignored either. Those are ciphertext,
#  and git is the only channel that reaches the far side, so they have to travel
#  in the repo. The passphrase never does - it lives outside this repo, mode
#  0600, and is defined on each machine by hand with `./secret.sh key`.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances ---------------------------------
.git-token
.heliograph-passphrase
*passphrase*
pat.txt
*.pat
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*credential*
*secret*.json
*secrets*.yml
*secrets*.yaml
kubeconfig
.kube/

# --- terraform ---------------------------------------------------------------
# State can hold secrets in plaintext and is never this repo's to own.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
tfplan
*.tfplan

# --- ansible -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.retry
.vault_pass
vault_pass.txt
fact_cache/

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
*~

# --- editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- agent state (local to each control node, never shared) ------------------
.station.lock
.station-state
# The step hashes `./station.sh --pin` approved. LOCAL on purpose: an approval
# recorded in this repo could be edited from the far side, which is the only
# side a pin exists to distrust.
.station-approved
# service.sh's runtime state when it falls back to setsid + nohup.
.agent-service.pid
.station-service.log
# How run.sh tells station.sh whether the finished log actually got out, so the
# loop can publish `idle` or `undelivered`. Local: it describes this machine's
# last delivery attempt and means nothing to anybody else.
.station-delivery
# The relay transport's sequence numbers. Freshness rests on these, so they are
# never shared and never committed: a copy restored elsewhere would let the
# relay replay everything it has ever seen.
.station-relay-state
# The transport's variables for a detached service - see service.sh. Mode 600,
# and it holds a token: never committed.
.station-env
